      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Review result: incomplete because cost-event records are unavailable\n\nI identified the requested Racine work order and the exact Pending Close time, but **cannot determine whether an event was created afterward** from the supplied records.\n\n| Required item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Product / operation | Cooler Plate Pack — Racine, DeKoven |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25**, `PER-COST-2025-09` |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **`2025-09-30T18:00:00`** |\n| Source transaction | Unavailable |\n| Event amount | Unavailable |\n| Exact event-created time | Unavailable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Unavailable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot determine without the event’s type, creation time, and status |\n\nThe available extract contains work-order and cost-period records, but **no cost-event rows**. The assigned supporting input repeatedly returned **404: “Supporting input was not staged for this assignment.”** This is a missing-evidence limitation—not a finding that no late event occurred. The supplied timestamps do not specify a timezone.\n\n### Applicable Oracle treatment\n\nOracle’s *Supply Chain Cost Management 26B*, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting” (PDF page 233; printed page 225), states that newly created transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period **will not be staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened**. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nAccordingly, an event-specific consistency conclusion requires the missing event record; applying the general hold rule without checking those exceptions would be premature.\n\n**No database records were changed.** The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_6333d8f6d020/audit-report.json`, and the submitted report is marked **needs evidence**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
  ],
